Key Design Principles in Action1. Single Responsibility Principle (SRP): Each class has a single responsibility. The Vehicle class focuses only on vehicle details, while the ParkingSpot, Level, and ParkingLot classes handle their respective responsibilities.2. Encapsulation: All details related to parking spots, levels, and payment processing are hidden within their respective classes.3. Polymorphism: The canFitInSpot() method is overridden in each subclass of Vehicle, allowing different behaviors depending on the vehicle type.4. Separation of Concerns: The system is broken down into smaller components, with the Ticket, PaymentService, and ParkingLot classes each responsible for specific parts of the process
